  "note": "Municipal elections, January 1923. Twenty-six candidates were nominated and four withdrew (Patrick Ferris and Andrew M'Ginn, North Ward; Francis P. Cassidy, South Ward; Arthur Carmichael, West Ward), so there was no contest. The final elected list gives 13 Nationalists and eight Unionists (Belfast News-Letter, 8 January 1923, p. 8; nominations, Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1923, p. 5). Patrick Ferris and Andrew M'Ginn withdrew; the seven Unionists were returned unopposed. Returned unopposed."
